## 7. Print a String Recursively

```c
#include <stdio.h>

void print(const char *);

int main()
{
    char s[20];
    printf("Enter a string:\n");
    scanf("%s", s);
    print(s);
    return 0;
}

void print(const char *p)
{
    if (*p)
    {
        printf("%c", *p);
        print(p + 1);      // try to avoid p++ here
    }
}
```

For `s = "abc"`: `print(100)` → `a`, `print(101)` → `b`, `print(102)` → `c`, `print(103)` → `'\0'` stops.

