## 8. Length of a String (`my_strlen`)

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int my_strlen(const char *);

int main()
{
    char s[20];
    printf("Enter a string:\n");
    scanf("%s", s);
    printf("%d\n", my_strlen(s));
    return 0;
}

int my_strlen(const char *p)
{
    if (*p)
        return 1 + my_strlen(p + 1);   // addition
    else
        return 0;
}
```

**Stack trace for `s = "abc"`** (addresses 100, 101, 102)

| Call | Condition | Returns |
|---|---|---|
| my_strlen(100) | `if (97)` ✔ | 1 + my_strlen(101) = 3 |
| my_strlen(101) | `if (98)` ✔ | 1 + my_strlen(102) = 2 |
| my_strlen(102) | `if (99)` ✔ | 1 + my_strlen(103) = 1 |
| my_strlen(103) | `if (0)` ✘ | 0 |

